# Stop-on-respawn guards for two stock-vendor HALs. Their .rc files live on the stock
# /vendor partition we ride and can't edit, but /product/etc/init is parsed AFTER /vendor
# so these stop triggers win (same approach as disable-ssdaemon.rc).
#
# 1. gto_secure_element_aidl_service (Thales/GTO HAL for the ST54 eSE = eSE1). Only the JP
#    SKU has a live eSE (Osaifu-Keitai / Suica, XDA #179): there the HAL registers and must
#    stay up, so it is NOT stopped on `running` any more (2026-09-19; the old running-stop is
#    what killed FeliCa). On other SKUs it exits at boot; stopping it on `restarting` breaks
#    the 5 s respawn loop (RescueParty flags_health_check storm, log flood, battery). The
#    framework side (com.android.se) probes a declared-but-absent eSE1 without blocking, so
#    SIM1/SIM2 OMAPI and OpenEUICC are unaffected either way.
#
# 2. ifaaaidl (vendor.zte.fingerprint.ifaaaidl-service): China-market IFAA biometric-pay
#    attestation HAL, restarting hundreds of times per boot. Not in any VINTF manifest,
#    unused here. The working Goodix UDFPS (ztecmdaidl) is a separate service.

on property:init.svc.gto_secure_element_aidl_service=restarting
    stop gto_secure_element_aidl_service

on property:init.svc.ifaaaidl=running
    stop ifaaaidl

on property:init.svc.ifaaaidl=restarting
    stop ifaaaidl
